# A rule with two reactant patterns that also deletes a bond.
#
# Split frees A from B when it meets a C. It writes "+" between A and B, so it
# may fire only if deleting the bond really leaves them in different complexes.
#
# The model holds two kinds of A.B pair, 100 of each. In a Ring pair A and B
# are joined a second time through their c sites, so deleting the b-a bond
# leaves them connected and Split must never fire on it: Ring stays at 100. In
# a Single pair the b-a bond is the only one, so Split does fire and Single
# falls to 0 by t=40.
#
# BioNetGen's network generator agrees. Given this model it produces one
# reaction, the one that splits the Single pair.
#
# NFsim used to apply this test only to rules with one reactant pattern, so
# Split broke every ring bond too.

begin model
begin parameters
  k  0.01
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(b,c)
  B(a,c)
  C(s)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(b!1,c!2).B(a!1,c!2)   100
  A(b!1,c).B(a!1,c)       100
  C(s)                    100
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules  Ring    A(b!1,c!2).B(a!1,c!2)
  Molecules  Single  A(b!1,c).B(a!1,c)
  Molecules  Cfree   C(s)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  Split: A(b!1).B(a!1) + C(s) -> A(b) + B(a) + C(s)   k
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
